# client-custom-fields.catalogue-cache-key.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: FE-3034 AC "Cache key carries an object-type axis, byte-identical at
# default" — the vue-query LIST key gains an `objectType` segment per catalogue,
# omitted at the client default. The plan's Correction 2: without it, two
# catalogues on the same client and brand collide on one cache entry and the
# second is served the first's rows.
#
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# Mutates: client-custom-fields.services.ts `loadList`'s `queryKey` — drops the
# conditional `objectType` segment, restoring the catalogue-blind key. The
# default consumer's key is unaffected (the segment was already omitted there),
# so this control fires only on the collision it exists to catch.
#
# Expected RED: client-custom-fields.catalogue.int.test.ts — the assertion that
# two catalogues resolved on the same client and brand hold SEPARATE rows (the
# invoice scope is not served the client scope's collection), plus the
# assertion that the client-default key still omits `objectType`.
#
# NOTE FOR THE PROVER: that spec does not exist on the branch this mutant ships
# with. Author it from the AC first (plan `docs/plans/FE-3034.md`, Testing
# Requirements: "the list key omits `object_type` at default and carries it per
# catalogue (no collision)"), then apply this blind.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>
#   pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/headless test client-custom-fields.catalogue.int   # must go RED
#   git apply -R <this file>
#
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.services.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/client-custom-fields.services.ts
index 9c11d2f7c..2f6163598 100644
